#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_payment_xendit
msgid ""
"# Xendit\n"
"\n"
"## Technical details\n"
"\n"
"APIs:\n"
"- [Invoices API](https://developers.xendit.co/api-reference/#create-invoice) version `2`\n"
"- [Credit Charge API](https://developers.xendit.co/api-reference/#create-charge) version `1`\n"
"\n"
"SDK: [Xendit.js](https://docs.xendit.co/credit-cards/integrations/tokenization)\n"
"\n"
"This module integrates Xendit with different payment flows depending on the payment method:\n"
"\n"
"- For `Card` payments, it renders a self-hosted payment form with regular (non-iframe) inputs and \n"
"  relies on the Xendit.js SDK to create a (single-use or multiple-use) token that is used to make\n"
"  the payment. When the payment is successful, and the user opts to save the payment method, the\n"
"  token is saved in Odoo. Other communications with Xendit are performed via server-to-server API\n"
"  calls.\n"
"\n"
"  The JS assets are loaded in JavaScript when the payment form is submitted.\n"
"\n"
"  As payment details are retrieved in clear but are immediately passed to the Xendit.js SDK, the\n"
"  solution qualifies for SAQ A-EP.\n"
"\n"
"- For other payment methods, this module uses the generic payment with redirection flow based on\n"
"  form submission provided by the `payment` module.\n"
"\n"
"This implementation allows supporting tokenization for `Card` payments whilst retaining support for\n"
"other payment methods via the redirection flow.\n"
"\n"
"## Supported features\n"
"\n"
"- Direct Payment flow for `Card` payment methods\n"
"- Payment with redirection flow for other payment methods\n"
"- Webhook notifications\n"
"- Tokenization with or without payment\n"
"\n"
"## Module history\n"
"\n"
"- `17.4`\n"
"  - The support for tokenization via `Card` is added. odoo/odoo#158445\n"
"- `17.0`\n"
"  - The first version of the module is merged. odoo/odoo#141661\n"
"\n"
"## Testing instructions\n"
"\n"
"https://developers.xendit.co/api-reference/#test-scenarios\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_project_task_device_visit
msgid ""
"# project_task_device_visit — Field Visit Reconciliation\n"
"\n"
"Crosses what an agronomist **declared** (a `project.task` with a customer and\n"
"a start date, in a project flagged *Reconcile Visits with GPS*) against where\n"
"their **vehicle** was (`device.client.visit`, the GPS parcel visits) and the\n"
"**attendance clock** (`hr.attendance`), and renders the weekly *Vehicle\n"
"Report* the Comercial area used to keep by hand in Excel.\n"
"\n"
"Not a lie detector: a reconciliation assistant. It confirms what it can\n"
"confirm and leaves the rest to human judgement. Every report opens with its\n"
"own coverage, so a \"62% confirmed\" is never read as \"62% comply\".\n"
"\n"
"## What it adds\n"
"\n"
"| Piece | Where |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| `gps_visit_tracking` on `project.project` | Project settings tab |\n"
"| `project.task.visit.report` — SQL view, one row per task and assignee | GPS ▸ Analysis ▸ Daily ▸ **Field Visits** (list, pivot, graph) |\n"
"| `project.task.visit.week.wizard` + QWeb report (HTML preview and landscape PDF) | GPS ▸ Analysis ▸ Daily ▸ **Vehicle Report (Weekly)** |\n"
"| `device.client.visit._rebuild_from_gps_logs()` + wizard | GPS ▸ Configuration ▸ **Rebuild Client Visits** (managers) |\n"
"\n"
"## Verdicts\n"
"\n"
"| Code | Rule |\n"
"|---|---|\n"
"| **A** | vehicle on the customer's parcel for at least `max(15% × allocated hours, 15 min)` |\n"
"| **A-** | entered the parcel, left before the threshold (drive-by) |\n"
"| **B** | GPS active that day, never entered the parcel — a question for the person, not a conclusion |\n"
"| **C** | not verifiable: no customer, customer without a parcel geofence, no tracked vehicle, or no positions that day |\n"
"| **T** | orthogonal flag: task created after 08:30 local of its own day |\n"
"\n"
"Constants (`REPORT_TZ`, `PLAN_CUTOFF`, `DWELL_RATIO`, `DWELL_FLOOR_MINUTES`)\n"
"live at the top of `reports/project_task_visit_report.py`. The threshold was\n"
"calibrated against measured visits; see the knowledge vault,\n"
"`workspaces/workspace-EVCA/loops/loop-actividades-agronomos/SKILL.md` §5.6.\n"
"\n"
"## Data flow\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"project.task ──employee_ids──▶ hr.employee ──stock.lot.operator_id──▶ device.device\n"
"      │                              │                                     │\n"
"      │ partner_id                   │ hr.attendance                       │ device.client.visit\n"
"      ▼                              ▼                                     ▼  device.data.log.gps\n"
"device.geo.fence (parcel)     clock in / out               parcel stays, GPS day bounds\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"* All source datetimes are UTC; a \"day\" is a local calendar day in\n"
"  `America/Mexico_City`.\n"
"* `device.client.visit` is written live by the 5-minute cron in\n"
"  `device_gps_geoengine`. History before the cron existed (or across an\n"
"  outage) is filled with **Rebuild Client Visits**, which replays the stored\n"
"  positions through the same 50 m proximity rule. A silence shorter than six\n"
"  hours inside a parcel does not end a visit: the tracker sleeps when parked.\n"
"* `employee_ids` is the canonical assignment in this fork (`project_hr`);\n"
"  `user_ids` only mirrors it.\n"
"\n"
"## Deploying\n"
"\n"
"1. Install the module.\n"
"2. Tick *Reconcile Visits with GPS* on the work-plan projects.\n"
"3. Run *Rebuild Client Visits* once over the period you want history for.\n"
"\n"
"## Tests\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"odoo-bin -c <conf> -d <db> -u project_task_device_visit --test-tags /project_task_device_visit --stop-after-init\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Needs PostGIS (the parcel match is `ST_DWithin` on `device_geo_fence.the_geom`).\n"
msgstr ""

